Found by reading bin/skeid and Proxy.pm (2026-09-29), not reproduced end to end.

bin/skeid builds Mojo::Server::Daemon / Prefork without inactivity_timeout and Proxy.pm sets none per request. Mojolicious 9.49 defaults to 30s. The upstream UA has request_timeout 300. A non-streamed completion that takes longer than 30s, or a stream whose first token takes longer than 30s, would be cut by Skeid itself.

Wanted: the client side waits at least as long as the upstream is allowed to take. Decide where it belongs (server option in bin/skeid vs. per-request $c->inactivity_timeout in the proxy handlers -- the latter also covers embedders of build_app), make it configurable next to the existing ENV surface, document it in POD/README. Reproduce with a scaled-down timeout in a test; no real 30s waits in t/.

Commit-ready in /home/getty/dev/langertha-skeid/.claude/worktrees/agent-abf915752cef2c0c3. Confirmed by red test (t/61-upstream-timeout.t), plus the user agent's own 40s inactivity default. SKEID_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT (default 300) drives upstream request and inactivity timeout; client connection gets server timeout + that, per request, on upstream routes only.

